                    </div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>

              <div class="sr-specs">
                <div class="sr-spec">
                  <h4>Display · Instrument Serif</h4>
                  <p class="sr-fig">
                    Nothing you say<br />
                    is <em>kept</em> after<br />
                    you close the tab.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    The italic is not decoration: it is the one place the brand’s voice rises. It
                    appears once per composition, on the phrase that carries the promise.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div class="sr-spec">
                  <h4>Reading · Inter Tight 17 / 1.62</h4>
                  <p>
                    A conversation is not a form. Serenica opens with a person, not a questionnaire —
                    no risk score, no drop-down for what is wrong, no “reason for your visit”. You
                    arrive, someone says hello by name, and the hour belongs to you.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    Everything a listener needs is held in the session and destroyed with it. There is
                    no case file to inherit, no note that follows you to a second conversation, and no
                    transcript in an inbox somewhere.
                  </p>
                  <p class="sr-lbl">
                    Labels are sentence case, 12.5px, second ink, no letter-spacing, no uppercase, no
                    monospace. If a label needs tracking to be legible, it is the wrong label.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div class="sr-spec">
                  <h4>Figures · tabular, right-aligned</h4>
                  <table>
                    <thead>
                      <tr><th>Week</th><th class="num">Sessions</th><th class="num">Median wait</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                      <tr><td>12 Oct</td><td class="num">1,842</td><td class="num">4m 02s</td></tr>
                      <tr><td>19 Oct</td><td class="num">1,977</td><td class="num">4m 18s</td></tr>
                      <tr><td>26 Oct</td><td class="num">2,104</td><td class="num">4m 10s</td></tr>
                      <tr><td>02 Nov</td><td class="num">1,918</td><td class="num">3m 55s</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
                <div class="sr-spec">
                  <h4>The field stamp</h4>
                  <p style="font-family: var(--sr-font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.9;">
                    Field 01 · six ridges · seed 3 · 1:1<br />
                    14 primitives · 3 published fails<br />
                    Case 23 · v1.0 · 2026
                  </p>
                  <p class="sr-lbl">
                    Mono is legal in exactly four places on this page. It is never a hero label, a nav
                    link or a colophon — those are set in the reading face at a size someone reads.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 06 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <section id="kit" class="sr-sec">
